Take a look in the save directory for the game, if you can find it.
Hopefully you will see something that has your character name.
For example, on the system I play on:

10586Bozo.Z   756tim.Z     11690christma.Z

The number is something associated with your account number.
The `Z` says the save file is compressed.  I get the impression
that since it says your game is "already in progress", that
the save file did not get around to compressing when it crashed.
In that case, your save file won't have the '.Z' on it.

Get your local nethack wizard (who ever installed the game)
to compress your save file.  Your character should be okay.
You might have lost a few dungeon levels along the way, but
your explorations will discover dungeons for you.  I just recall
the last time I had a character crash, it was restored with the
character completely the way I remembered him, but the Gnomish
Mines had to be completely explored a second time.

Hope this helps.

Roger Christman


